      "message": "**1\\. Unchecked BoringSSL API Return Values (`bootrom.cc`)** In `aes_gcm_encrypt_openssl` and `aes_gcm_decrypt_openssl`, the return values for `EVP_EncryptUpdate`, `EVP_EncryptFinal_ex`, `EVP_DecryptUpdate`, and `EVP_CIPHER_CTX_ctrl` are completely ignored.\n\n* **Risk:** If BoringSSL encounters an internal error or context issue, these functions can fail silently, leaving the output buffer uninitialized or containing partial data. In an encryption context, this can lead to transmitting corrupted data or bypassing authentication.  \n* **Remediation:** Check the return value (usually `1` for success) of every `EVP_*` call. If any call fails, clean up the context and return `false`.",
